# jetstream2.config -- machine/layout config for the WoC extraction pipeline.
# Sourced by the bash tools (runExo.sh, deOffend.sh, deOffendWatch.sh) and
# parsed as KEY=VALUE by wocFixErr.py. Keep values literal (no $-expansion) so
# both shells and Python read them the same way. Override the file location
# with the WOC_CONFIG environment variable.
#
# Disk layout on this Jetstream2 instance:
#   * TREES ($VOL/trees) is a large ~40TB volume holding the bare repo clones
#     (git clone --mirror) for one or more versions at a time -- this is by far
#     the biggest consumer, hence its own large disk.
#   * Dumps go to two smaller ~5TB volumes, $VOL/out and $VOL/b (DUMP_DIRS).
#     A given batch/version writes its {blob,commit,tree,tag}.{idx,bin} to one
#     of them; both fill up as runs proceed, so a dataset's dumps may be on
#     either disk (the tools resolve which per dataset). Once a version's dumps
#     are rsynced to da8 and STAGE=verified, its clones and dumps are deleted to
#     free space for the next versions.
VOL=/media/volume                            # base of the mounted volumes
TREES=/media/volume/trees                    # bare repo clones (large disk)
DUMP_DIRS="out b"                            # dump subdirs under $VOL (per batch)
AGG_REPO_MIN=30000000000                  # 30GB - max a repo may contribute (per-shard AND aggregate)
RSYNC_DEST=da8:/mnt/ordos/data/data/update   # rsync target root (per-version /$ver appended)
HASOBJ_HOST=da5                              # host running cleanBlb|hasObj for todo dedup
KEEP_FILE=/media/volume/trees/keep         # allowlist: repos never excluded (one per line)
OFFENDERS=/media/volume/trees/offenders      # offender registry
